    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0834" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.927/45</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1924</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 17.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 495</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing my number 38 of May 27th, 6
                        p.m.,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d662-f1"/> I have the honor to herewith enclose
                    a copy of the full text of the decision rendered in regard to the Antiquities
                    Law. I am at the same time enclosing a copy of my <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Aide-Mémoire</hi> on this question, dated April 22, 1924.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d662-f2"/></p>
                <p>I may state that on April 26th, I saw the Minister of Public Works who controls
                    for the time being this matter, and made a strenuous effort to have this
                    question remain exactly as it was during the year 1922–1923, but I was unable to
                    do so. It will be seen, however, that no reference is made to the Lacau
                    proposition, that is to say, leaving the decision wholly in the hands of Lacau
                    to say whether or not there shall be a division of any of the articles
                    found.</p>
                <p>I shall be glad to discuss this question further with the Department and with the
                    Metropolitan Museum when I am in the States.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Morton Howell</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d662-a1.xml" xpointer="d662-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d662-a2.xml" xpointer="d662-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
